node_modules/
dist/
src-tauri/target/
# `gen/schemas` is regenerated from the command list on every build and is
# nobody's to edit. `gen/android` is not: `tauri android init` writes it once
# and then it is ours — the manifest carries decisions (allowBackup is off,
# because the Keystore key behind the credential store is never backed up) that
# exist nowhere else. Ignoring the whole of `gen/` meant those decisions lived
# only on the machine that made them and would come back as the template's
# defaults on the next checkout, with nothing to say they had been considered.
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
*.local
